                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="13695245" author="smarthi" created="Fri, 28 Jun 2013 03:55:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue is only seen when running with Complimentary Naive Bayes or Naive Bayes options.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;seqdirectory now executes as a MapReduce job (in light of the changes in Mahout-833) unless the sequential option is explicitly specified.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;classify-20newsgroups.sh creates 20new-seq/ directory on the first run, but subsequent runs fail as the directory already exists from the previous runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix was to specify --overwrite flag when invoking seqdirectory.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="13695251" author="hudson" created="Fri, 28 Jun 2013 04:15:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Integrated in Mahout-Quality #2115 (See &lt;a href=&quot;https://builds.apache.org/job/Mahout-Quality/2115/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://builds.apache.org/job/Mahout-Quality/2115/&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;
